    <summary>A local-first AI assistant that floats on top of your desktop.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Floaty lives in your tray and as a draggable swimming-ring overlay that stays on top of your other
windows. Through the ring you can capture what's on your screen - a screenshot plus the actual text
content read via accessibility APIs - and everything you capture is embedded into a local memory
that the assistant can search when you chat with it.

Everything stays on your machine: memory, conversations, skills, settings and speech-to-text all
live in `%USERPROFILE%\.floaty`. The only thing that leaves your computer is what you send to the
LLM provider you configure - and with on-device embeddings plus a local model in Ollama, nothing
has to.

### Features

* Floating ring overlay - draggable, borderless, always on top, click-through where it is transparent
* Screen capture that grabs a screenshot *and* the text of the active window via UI Automation
* Optional automatic screen history, redacted before it is written (password managers, private
  browsing windows and password fields are never captured)
* Local memory with on-device vector search over everything you captured
* Any model provider - OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Azure OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, Mistral, DeepSeek,
  xAI, Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
* On-device embeddings and fully local speech-to-text, so it can work with no API key at all
* Agent skills (`SKILL.md`) and Model Context Protocol servers

### Packaging notes

* Installs **per user** into `%LocalAppData%\Floaty`. No elevation, and the app is only available to
  the account that ran `choco install`.
* Floaty updates itself via Velopack when it starts, so the version Chocolatey reports can lag
  behind the version actually installed. Run `choco pin add -n=floaty` if you would rather
  Chocolatey left it alone.
* Your data in `%USERPROFILE%\.floaty` is **not** removed when the package is uninstalled.
* Windows x64 only.
]]></description>
